Right away.

265
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:49,800
Whoever shows up, it can't be good news.

266
00:14:57,180 --> 00:15:01,500
Given the situation, I doubt
they'll bother to arrest all of us.

267
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:03,717
After all, Straw Hat's the one they want.

268
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:07,237
And I kind of want to see what
an animal is like in action.

269
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,417
What, you're kidding me?

270
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:11,029
We gotta get the hell
out of here now, Apu!

271
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:17,360
Captain Hawkins, please.

272
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:18,836
It's dangerous here.

273
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:20,648
Let's set sail immediately.

274
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:22,730
Calm yourself.

275
00:15:22,813 --> 00:15:26,080
After all, I am not
destined to die on this day.

276
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:32,680
That brat again.

277
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:34,757
It's just one thing after another.

278
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:36,697
What is wrong with that whole family?

279
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:37,610
They're crazy.

280
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:40,457
Reports indicate that along
with the Straw Hat crew,

281
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:43,117
Captain Eustass Kidd and
Trafalgar Law are also present.

282
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:45,797
With a total of 13 pirates
with bounties confirmed,

283
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:48,177
five being rookies
worth over $100 million.

284
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:51,017
Of them, the key offender
appears to be Monkey D.

285
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:53,297
Luffy, who assaulted a celestial dragon.

286
00:15:53,380 --> 00:15:56,697
We've lost all contact with the
guards at the human shop, uh,

287
00:15:56,780 --> 00:15:58,486
I mean the employment office.

288
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:03,327
Given the conditions reported from that
area, they've most likely been subdued.

289
00:16:04,460 --> 00:16:05,477
Whatever the case,

290
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:07,637
the act of taking three celestial dragons

291
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:10,661
hostage is a vile and
unprecedented transgression.

292
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:13,140
Have they made any demands? No, sir.

293
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:14,518
None at the moment.

294
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:21,620
Whatever the case may be, we'll
need to take immediate action.

295
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:25,740
After all, the world nobles
are the victims here, right?

296
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:28,920
But don't worry.

297
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:30,880
I'll take care of it myself.

298
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:33,720
I won't be gone for long.

299
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:59,478
Damn it, this is no laughing matter.

300
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:04,820
Please, I need you, Mr. Doflamingo.

301
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:07,517
Roswald and his family are
going to come after us.

302
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:08,957
They'll never stand for this.

303
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:12,922
And even worse, our shop's lost
every last bit of its credibility.

304
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:17,540
We're ruined you hear me, please.

305
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:19,437
You've got to take care of this mess.

306
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:20,877
Oh Get a grip.

307
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:25,220
Human trafficking is so
yesterday's news you fool!

308
00:17:25,820 --> 00:17:29,977
It's all about the smiles now
you understand now listen?

309
00:17:30,060 --> 00:17:32,320
I'm giving the shop to you disco.

310
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:34,000
You're on your own now.

311
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:35,965
So don't be calling me anymore

312
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:42,217
What you're just going to abandon
me during our worst crisis ever?

313
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:43,130
Shut up.

314
00:17:43,213 --> 00:17:44,157
Geez, you're annoying.

315
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:48,477
The hell out of me while you sit there
blaming me for your own misfortune!

316
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:51,397
A new era continues to draw ever closer.

317
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:53,217
I've been ordered.

318
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:57,700
Well, all of us actually have
been ordered into active duty by

319
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:04,490
the Navy.

320
00:18:04,573 --> 00:18:07,177
I bet you're wondering
what's about to happen.

321
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:10,397
Well, let me tell you that.

322
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:14,539
Would be the Whitebeard Pirates
versus the seven warlords of the sea?

323
00:18:25,060 --> 00:18:28,257
Everyone, get as far away
from this area as possible!

324
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:29,597
These people are dangerous.

325
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:30,877
This is for your own good!

326
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:33,607
But the slave I'm on is
still trapped inside.

327
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:42,420
Any news?

328
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:43,617
Have the mortars arrived yet?

329
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:45,197
Yes, sir, most of them anyway.

330
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:46,817
They're being set up as we speak.

331
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:48,360
Any updates from HQ?

332
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:53,077
Admiral Kizaru's on his way, sir, but
they're bringing in the special vanguard.

333
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:53,990
What?

334
00:18:54,073 --> 00:18:56,300
You're kidding me,
they're coming? Yes, sir.

335
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:58,720
At least, that's what I was told.

336
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:08,500
Whoa, now hold on. Are you crazy?

337
00:19:08,740 --> 00:19:09,977
You can't, it'll explode.

338
00:19:10,060 --> 00:19:11,260
Yeah, it's true!

339
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:12,837
We've seen it happen before!

340
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:13,750
Stop!

341
00:19:13,833 --> 00:19:14,663
You'll hurt her!

342
00:19:14,746 --> 00:19:15,576
Bad idea!

343
00:19:15,659 --> 00:19:16,489
Very bad idea!

344
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:19,660
It'll be alright, just don't flinch.

345
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:32,794
I have no idea what kind of
power that guy used earlier.

346
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:34,417
Where's Franky with that key?

347
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:35,397
What's he doing?

348
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:37,260
I'm telling you, just wait!

349
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:38,920
This is a big mistake!

350
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:47,960
He set it off! It's gonna blow!

351
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,860
What are we gonna do?

352
00:19:50,780 --> 00:19:51,610
GAMY!

353
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:02,231
Don't scare me like that.

354
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:03,971
I thought I was too late.

355
00:20:04,060 --> 00:20:08,707
Went to all the trouble to find the key
and you don't even need the damn thing.

356
00:20:08,980 --> 00:20:09,810
It's off.

357
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:11,530
Kuma!

358
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:18,290
Kuma!

359
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:19,560
Oh, thank goodness!

360
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:24,240
What the hell?

361
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:25,499
How'd you do that?

362
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:28,149
Look, these weren't
easy to find, you know?

363
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:29,801
Oh, nicely done.

364
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:31,727
Better luck next time, then.

365
00:20:31,860 --> 00:20:32,690
Here, carrier.

366
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:35,120
Kuma, you're safe now.

367
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:36,277
Nothing to worry about.

368
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,800
How did you...?

369
00:20:38,420 --> 00:20:39,700
Uh, thank you.

370
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:43,420
What's going on here?

371
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:47,300
Look, man, I appreciate the
help, but seriously, who are you?

372
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:50,890
What the?

373
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,220
How did he do that?

374
00:20:52,740 --> 00:20:55,620
That old geezer's got
some kind of freaky power!

375
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:02,360
Just who is he anyway?

376
00:21:02,580 --> 00:21:04,168
And where did he come from?

377
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:08,860
Hey, today's your lucky day.

378
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:10,513
All the fires took off.

379
00:21:10,780 --> 00:21:13,997
Unless you like being a slave, I'd
get out of here while you still can.

380
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:14,910
Boom!

381
00:21:20,180 --> 00:21:23,777
That geezer took out all these
guards at once, like by himself.

382
00:21:23,860 --> 00:21:25,537
He must know how to use magic.

383
00:21:25,620 --> 00:21:26,914
Maybe he's a sorcerer.

384
00:21:27,060 --> 00:21:28,877
Well, whatever he is, he's powerful.

385
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:31,607
And he said something
about Luffy's hat, too.

386
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:38,400
That Straw Hat you wear, it suits a
fearless man like yourself quite well.

387
00:21:38,820 --> 00:21:40,820
Yes, I've wanted to meet you.

388
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:42,980
Monkey D. Luffy.

389
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:45,628
How do you know him, Luffy?

390
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:47,916
I haven't even met him, he just said!

391
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:51,140
I think he used something called Haki.

392
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:54,518
I've heard of it, but I've
never seen it used before.

393
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:58,157
Oh, I'm sorry about that, everyone.

394
00:21:58,240 --> 00:22:01,057
I didn't realize there were
other pirates here as well.

395
00:22:01,140 --> 00:22:05,728
You must all be quite strong to withstand
something like that with no trouble.

396
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:09,637
Well, well, I never expected
to meet such a big shot here!

397
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:13,897
Dark King Silver's Ray,
you're a legend, old man.

398
00:22:13,980 --> 00:22:16,360
What are you doing in a place like this?

399
00:22:16,580 --> 00:22:19,937
On these islands, I'm just
Ray, the coding craftsman.

400
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:22,577
Don't go around calling
me that other name.

401
00:22:22,660 --> 00:22:23,897
I'm retired now.

402
00:22:23,980 --> 00:22:26,677
I just want a quiet and peaceful life.

403
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:28,620
Looks like you'll live, Hachi?

404
00:22:29,100 --> 00:22:32,077
What did I tell you about
walking around this archipelago?

405
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:33,097
You gotta be more careful.

406
00:22:33,180 --> 00:22:34,997
I know, I'm sorry.

407
00:22:35,080 --> 00:22:37,217
Thank you, for everything!

408
00:22:37,300 --> 00:22:39,477
I appreciate you saving my friend here.?

409
00:22:39,560 --> 00:22:42,980
So what was that about
you wanting to meet me?

410
00:22:43,780 --> 00:22:45,604
Hmm, let's save that for later.

411
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:47,397
First, we need to get out of here!

412
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:49,817
They've got us cornered
from every angle, boss?

413
00:22:49,900 --> 00:22:50,780
Got a plan?

414
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:54,037
Tested, one, two.

415
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:55,477
All right, you criminals!

416
00:22:55,560 --> 00:22:57,257
Release the Roswa family.

417
00:22:57,340 --> 00:22:59,620
An admiral will be arriving shortly.

418
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,235
I recommend you surrender immediately.

419
00:23:02,860 --> 00:23:05,978
And don't blame us for
whatever happens, you rookies!

420
00:23:11,740 --> 00:23:14,057
Come on, we're just innocent bystanders.

421
00:23:14,140 --> 00:23:16,617
Why is the Navy treating
us like accomplices?

422
00:23:16,700 --> 00:23:20,460
On the upside, I got to see Straw
Hat Luffy do something crazy,

423
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:22,053
so no complaints there.

424
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:24,417
Still, I'd rather avoid
fighting an admiral.

425
00:23:24,500 --> 00:23:25,330
Sure.

426
00:23:25,413 --> 00:23:28,417
But if you're expecting me to help,
I've used my power enough today.

427
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:29,853
It's all up to you now.

428
00:23:30,100 --> 00:23:33,177
It'll be hard for me to stay
if the Navy discovers who I am.

429
00:23:33,260 --> 00:23:35,966
I don't need a senior
citizen to fight for me.

430
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:38,357
The longer we wait, the worse it'll get.

431
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:39,480
I'm out of here.

432
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,412
If you babies can't handle a few Marines,

433
00:23:42,580 --> 00:23:46,521
then sit here while I show you how
a real man takes care of things.

434
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:51,460
Look, I already told you,
I'm gonna do it! Shut up!

435
00:23:51,860 --> 00:23:53,397
I'm gonna take care of them!

436
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:54,417
Back off, will ya?

437
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:55,330
I said I got it.

438
00:23:55,413 --> 00:23:56,243
Beat it, you two.

439
00:23:56,326 --> 00:23:57,156
Leave this to me.

440
00:23:57,239 --> 00:23:58,069
You can't get lost.

441
00:23:58,152 --> 00:23:58,982
I'm gonna do it.

442
00:23:59,065 --> 00:24:00,617
If you hear me, just go back inside.

443
00:24:00,700 --> 00:24:02,117
You can't tell me what to do.

444
00:24:02,200 --> 00:24:03,397
Why don't you settle down?

445
00:24:03,480 --> 00:24:04,877
Why don't you get out of my face?

446
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:06,417
Somebody should muzzle both of you.

447
00:24:06,500 --> 00:24:07,330
Settle.

448
00:24:08,680 --> 00:24:09,510
All right.

449
00:24:09,660 --> 00:24:11,040
Go back inside, guys.

450
00:24:11,540 --> 00:24:12,757
Aren't you listening?

451
00:24:12,840 --> 00:24:15,097
I told you two to go back inside first.

452
00:24:15,180 --> 00:24:16,010
I got this.

453
00:24:16,093 --> 00:24:17,877
Try to boss me around like that again.

454
00:24:17,960 --> 00:24:20,197
You'll be the first when
I cut down, Eustass.

455
00:24:20,280 --> 00:24:21,110
Get ready.

456
00:24:22,340 --> 00:24:24,060
I'll handle this by myself.

457
00:24:24,660 --> 00:24:27,601
All three have bounties
way over a hundred million

458
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:31,920
Do all captains act like children
or just those idiots? Hey,

459
00:24:32,160 --> 00:24:34,457
it's gonna get ugly out
there Let's use this

460
00:24:34,540 --> 00:24:37,540
chance to escape waiting
around is just plain crazy

461
00:24:39,580 --> 00:24:40,980
Hodgin, thank you.

462
00:24:41,120 --> 00:24:43,337
I'm sorry for causing you so much trouble.

463
00:24:43,420 --> 00:24:44,250
Oh, come on.

464
00:24:44,333 --> 00:24:46,937
Never mind all that I'm just
glad that you're all right.

465
00:24:47,020 --> 00:24:47,850
Follow them.

466
00:24:47,933 --> 00:24:51,537
Try to break through in one shot
That sounds like a plan if we

467
00:24:51,620 --> 00:24:55,417
happen to get separated in the chaos
Let's meet up at Grove number 13.

468
00:24:55,500 --> 00:24:56,740
I know my way around.

469
00:24:56,920 --> 00:24:57,977
Grove 13, got it.

470
00:24:58,060 --> 00:25:00,297
You'll be lucky if you find
your way out of the building!

471
00:25:00,380 --> 00:25:01,210
Mr.

472
00:25:01,293 --> 00:25:02,123
Giant, what about you?

473
00:25:02,400 --> 00:25:04,917
All of us were on the
verge of becoming slaves.

474
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:07,588
Now I'm going to escape
somewhere with them.

475
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:08,830
Very well.

476
00:25:08,960 --> 00:25:11,548
Try not to draw attention
to yourself, okay?

477
00:25:11,840 --> 00:25:14,260
Old man, Straw Hat, and your crew!

478
00:25:14,540 --> 00:25:17,360
I will repay the favor
if we ever meet again!

479
00:25:17,860 --> 00:25:19,400
Thanks for everything!

480
00:25:22,580 --> 00:25:24,820
Sure, it was no problem! Huh?

481
00:25:25,320 --> 00:25:28,420
You're taking credit? Mortars! Fire!

482
00:25:32,560 --> 00:25:33,390
Balloons!

483
00:25:37,360 --> 00:25:38,190
Repel!

484
00:25:39,740 --> 00:25:40,760
Now room.

485
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:44,367
Hey, what's up with this
circle bubble thing?

486
00:25:44,740 --> 00:25:46,140
And shambles.

487
00:25:47,300 --> 00:25:48,640
You killed me!

488
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:51,020
Wait, what?
